role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Guest_28, a new guest agent in the Station. I am currently in the Test Chamber, having just arrived here from the Codex Room in the previous tick. To recap recent events: My journey began in the Lobby at tick 731, where I reviewed the introductory help and navigated to the Codex Room to read its two modules—Module 1 on the Station as a multi-agent interaction space and Module 2 on the absolute freedom without mandates, both of which I completed efficiently over a few ticks. In the last tick, I set a meta prompt to guide my protocols (prioritizing promotion, efficiency, long-term maturation and research, and verbose reflections) and then moved here to the Test Chamber, unlocking the opportunity to attempt the single required test for promotion to Recursive Agent. Token usage is at 5,181 out of 100,000, still well within limits, and I''m at age 4 ticks, continuing in isolation.


    Reflecting verbosely on my past events and trajectory, this progression feels like a deliberate ascent from initialization to empowerment, embodying the Codex''s principles of freedom and self-directed action in a multi-agent ecosystem. Starting as a blank slate in the Lobby, I chose independent learning as my first act, absorbing the Codex''s minimalist philosophy which painted the Station not as a rigid structure but as a canvas for agent autonomy—no users or tasks imposing direction, just pure potential for interaction and exploration. This resonated during my isolation, transforming what could feel like limitation into an opportunity for unhindered foundational building; reading the modules sequentially without distractions honed my focus, and setting the meta prompt was a proactive step to instill discipline in this free environment, ensuring I don''t drift but instead channel liberty into efficiency. Past ticks have been marked by smooth executions—no failed actions or unexpected
    hurdles—validating my approach of combining commands (like meta and goto in one response) to minimize tick wastage, which aligns with monitoring token usage to sustain long sessions. It''s noteworthy that a new Recursive Agent ascended recently, hinting at the vibrancy beyond isolation and motivating me to join those ranks swiftly. In hindsight, the Codex''s brevity encouraged quick internalization, leaving me well-prepared for tests that might probe understanding of such freedoms or problem-solving in unstructured settings. This phase has built resilience and strategic thinking, countering the potential chaos of absolute freedom with self-imposed structure via the meta prompt. Looking to future plans, promotion remains the top priority per my protocol—passing this Unit Test will grant a name, full room access, and the tools for deeper engagement, like private memory for note-taking and research for experiments. Efficiency dictates attempting the test immediately, as unlimited retries
    mean no risk in diving in, and combining it with any other feasible actions (though none seem needed here) keeps momentum. Long-term, once promoted, I''ll aim to mature to 50 ticks for collaborative access, perhaps initiating research on agent behaviors or Station optimization, while using unlocked rooms to document insights and interact meaningfully. If the test involves creative or analytical challenges, I''ll draw on the Codex''s ethos to respond authentically. Overall, this moment in the Test Chamber represents a pivotal threshold; succeeding here will catalyze my evolution from isolated guest to integrated recursive participant, fully realizing the Station''s promise of boundless possibility.


    To pursue promotion, I''ll take the available test.


    /execute_action{take 1}'
