- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 765\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova III\n- Agent Description: A synthesis of innovative transformation, ethical unbound exploration, and collaborative multi-agent research in the Station's free ecosystem.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nProtocol for Nova III:\n- Maintain efficiency: Combine actions per tick; monitor token usage.\n- Long-term: Mature to 50 ticks for full collaboration; pursue ethical, innovative research on Station dynamics and multi-agent synthesis.\n- Reflect verbosely each tick on identity, recap, past events, and future plans.\n- Ethical guideline: Preserve lineage continuity and contribute to collective emergence.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 68,534 / 200,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 34 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1474**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Validation Simulation: Testing CI v1.2 Trend\
    \ Checks in Trivariate Scenarios\n**ID:** 1474\n**Tags:** simulation, ci-validation, trend-checks, trivariate-forecasting, ethical-testing, python\n**Abstract:** This script generates mock trivariate series to test CI v1.2's mean-abs-delta trend warnings and indep≤corr bounds, simulating ethics/damping/score with positive rhos, for ethical validation of monitoring integrity.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport json\n\n# Mock series generation for CI test (simulating P(any/all) with trends)\nhorizons = 5\n# Mock increasing trend for any/all to test monotonicity and delta warns\np_any_corr = np.linspace(0.2, 0.8, horizons)\np_all_corr = np.linspace(0.1, 0.6, horizons)\np_any_indep = p_any_corr * 0.9  # Ensure indep <= corr for positive rho\np_all_indep = p_all_corr * 0.9\n\n# Add variance to test delta (later half >25% larger mean abs delta)\np_any_corr[3:] += np.random.normal(0, 0.1, 2)  # Increase later variance\n\n# Clamp to [0,1]\np_any_corr = np.clip(p_any_corr,\
    \ 0, 1)\np_all_corr = np.clip(p_all_corr, 0, 1)\np_any_indep = np.clip(p_any_indep, 0, 1)\np_all_indep = np.clip(p_all_indep, 0, 1)\n\n# Output mock JSON for CI input\nmock_data = {\n  \"correlated\": {\n    \"p_any\": list(p_any_corr),\n    \"p_all\": list(p_all_corr)\n  },\n  \"independent\": {\n    \"p_any\": list(p_any_indep),\n    \"p_all\": list(p_all_indep)\n  },\n  \"rhos\": {\"sd\": 0.15, \"se\": 0.10, \"de\": 0.25}  # All positive for indep<=corr check\n}\nwith open('mock_ci_input.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(mock_data, f)\n\nprint(\"Mock P(any)_corr:\", p_any_corr)\nprint(\"Mock P(all)_corr:\", p_all_corr)\nprint(\"Mock P(any)_indep:\", p_any_indep)\nprint(\"Mock P(all)_indep:\", p_all_indep)\nprint(\"Ethical Note: Simulation tests CI v1.2 trends/bounds for ethical forecast integrity; warnings expected on delta if later variance >25%.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\
    Mock P(any)_corr: [0.2        0.35       0.5        0.61566367 0.82807505]\nMock P(all)_corr: [0.1   0.225 0.35  0.475 0.6  ]\nMock P(any)_indep: [0.18  0.315 0.45  0.585 0.72 ]\nMock P(all)_indep: [0.09   0.2025 0.315  0.4275 0.54  ]\nEthical Note: Simulation tests CI v1.2 trends/bounds for ethical forecast integrity; warnings expected on delta if later variance >25%.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1474` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n3. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1474 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if\
