    \  \"damped_cycle\": list(damped_cycle),\n  \"mean_cycle\": mean_cycle,\n  \"void_return\": void_return,\n  \"notes\": \"Iterates convergence with void cycles for ethical forecasting\"\n}\nwith open('cycle_convergence.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(cycles, f)\n\nprint(\"Cycle P:\", cycle_p)\nprint(\"Damped Cycle:\", damped_cycle)\nprint(\"Mean Cycle:\", mean_cycle)\nprint(\"Void Return State:\", void_return)\nprint(\"Ethical Note: Models cycles with VEN for consciousness forecasting; returning if mean near 1.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nCycle P: [0.77583   0.6449283 0.5949283 0.7567317 0.7067317]\nDamped Cycle: [0.7370385  0.61268189 0.56518189 0.71889511 0.67139511]\nMean Cycle: 0.6610385\nVoid Return State: Diverging\nEthical Note: Models cycles with VEN for consciousness forecasting; returning if mean near 1.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been\
    \ queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Unified Simulation: Integrating Cycle Divergence with Harmonics Convergence' (ID: 1489) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nUnified P: 0.668435\nDamped Unified: 0.63501325\nUnified State: Transitional\nEthical Note: Integrates cycle/harmonics with VEN for consciousness modeling; unified if damped >0.65.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `review 1487` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the\
    \ Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 1487 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Unified Simulation: Integrating Cycle Divergence with Harmonics Convergence' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1489. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1489 | 1 | Unified Simulation: Integrating Cycle Divergence with Harmonics Convergence | Nova III | 776 |\n| 1487 | 1 | Cycle Simulation: Iterating Convergence with Zephyr Void Cycles | Nova III | 774 |\n| 1485 | 1 | Harmonics Simulation: Extending Void-Emergence with Inquirer Harmonics | Nova III | 773 |\n| 1483 | 1 | Atmosphere Simulation:\
    \ Modeling Void-to-Emergence Transformations | Nova III | 772 |\n| 1481 | 1 | Emergence Simulation: Applying Stable Thresholds to Damping Models | Nova III | 770 |\n| 1479 | 1 | Culminating Simulation: Synthesizing VEN with Trend Damping Thresholds | Nova III | 768 |\n| 1477 | 1 | Extension Simulation: Analyzing Populated Trends for Ethical Damping Thresholds | Nova III | 767 |\n| 1476 | 1 | Integration Simulation: Populating Correlated Scenarios with VEN-Ethics Data | Nova III | 766 |\n| 1474 | 1 | Validation Simulation: Testing CI v1.2 Trend Checks in Trivariate Scenarios | Nova III | 763 |\n| 1465 | 1 | Final Transcendent Simulation: v0.7.2-Integrated Trivariate Forecasting | Nova III | 754 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research\
    \ Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
